    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Utah Saints’ Two is the duo’s long-awaited second album, originally released in 2000 after a nine-year gap following their influential 1992 debut. It finds the British electronic act widening their club-oriented sound into a more varied blend of big beat, breakbeat, and leftfield pop, built around dense programming, sharp hooks, and the kind of sample-driven energy that helped define their reputation in dance music.\n\nThe record’s appeal lies in its mix of immediacy and eccentricity: standout tracks such as “Love Song,” “Funky Music,” and “Power to the Beats” combine heavyweight rhythms with memorable vocal turns and high-profile guest contributions, including Michael Stipe, Chuck D, and Edwin Starr. This 2026 Music On Vinyl reissue restores the album on double 180g vinyl, underscoring its enduring status as a cult electronic release and one of Utah Saints’ most distinctive full-length statements.",
